 a scarf, a top hat, two stick arms, a carrot nose, and a small robin perched on his head\nmake the kite 30 wide and 45 high\nset star yellow pointy small\npleeeease make the clouds fluffy again\ncould you show me where the treasure chest is\nfirst the barn, then the silo, then the windmill at the far right\ncan you make it look like the dog is running? just add motion lines\nadd three apples on the ground and a ladder against the tree\nI wonder if the hill should be behind the house — try it\nwtaer the flowers, they look wilted\nmake the rowboat row straight toward the pier\nput a wizard at the cave mouth: tall hat, long beard, a staff with a glowing crystal\nset wizard hat purple\nchange the dragons from red to green, one by one\nshow what the forest looked like before I asked for pines\ncould you move the caption to the bottom left\nthe girl skipping rope, the boy on the swing, the dog mid jump, and the cat asleep on the porch — put them all in the yard\nmake the moon a crescent instead of a full circle\nnext add a trail of footprints from the gate to the door\nits to dark make the street lighter pls\nset scene night sky stars\nset moon cream small\ndraw a river that widens toward the bottom of the page\ncan you make the house two stories tall\ninstead of a flat roof give it a gabled one\ntell me how many layers the drawing has right now\nplace the umbrella behind the bench, tilted, so it shelters the two cats\nagain, sorry — the left cat, not the right one\nmake it about 200 wide and 150 high, whatever fits the page\nthen label the pond\nremove the second sailboat; the first one can stay\nset label pond dark blue italic\nwhat if the cat chased the mouse instead of the ball\nput a cow, a sheep, and a chicken in the meadow — oh, and a farmer leaning on the gate\nmove the sun down a touch — that is all; then save it\nline the ducks up in a row facing left\nshow what changed\nmake the windmill look like it spins by adding little arcs near the blades\nits suposed to be autumn so color the tree orangey red\ncan you enlarge the whole thing by about a quarter\ndrop in a sunflower between the fence and the path\nset girl dress yellow shoes brown\nhvae the birds fly toward the mountain\ndraw the outline first, then fill it in\nmake the train six cars long with two windows per car\nthen put smoke curls above the chimney\ncould you check where the level crossing is\nadd a station platform with a bench, a sign, and two passengers waiting\nplease make the tracks curve gentler toward the right edge\nwhere did the crossing go? it vanished\nset the sign text 12 point bold\nan owl on the branch, a nest above it, three eggs inside, and a mouse peeking from the roots below — add all of that to the oak\nmake the cave mouth half as wide\ntop the birthday cake with seven candles\nput the balloon at x 120 y 40 and tie its string to the boy's hand\nI wonder if you could add a picket fence around the garden\nnext the tulips, then the daffodils, then the roses by the wall\npleese make the cloumns of the colonnade even\ntell me if anything overlaps the pond\nleave the leaves alone this time, just thin the branches\nset hut brown straw roof\nhand the fisherman a net and tilt his hat forward\ncan you make the rocket point straight up\nmake the rocket 12 wide and 40 high\nwhere should the flag go? ask me before placing it\nthen draw stars in decreasing size toward the corner\nadd two mice by the skirting board, one standing, one sitting up\ninstead of a motorboat make it a rowing boat with oars\nset truck cab red container gray\nput a lighthouse on the cliff, a keeper's cottage below it, a winding path between them, and gulls circling overhead\nI wonder if you could swap the seasons to early spring\nshow what changed in the last minute\nmake the castle: four towers, one gatehouse, a flag on each tower, and a moat all round\nhvae the flag flutter to the left\nremove the sheep that looks like a cloud\nnext clean up the stray lines near the horizon\ntell me where the well is supposed to be\ncolor the door teal and keep the walls cream\nset the swing rope brown seat gray\ncan you put a wheelbarrow next to the shed\nthe zebra grazing, the giraffe by the acacia, the lions resting under the shade, and a bird on the giraffe's back — put them all on the savanna\nmake the watering can green and lean it against the spade\nwhat if you tilted the picture slightly, like a photo taken in a hurry\ninstead of grass use sand around the pond\ndraw footprints leading off the bottom edge — that way the scene feels ongoing\npleese make the cloumns of smoke thinner\nset kite diamond red tail long\nthen again, maybe no tail at all\ncould you add a distant ship on the horizon, tiny\ntell me which colors you used for the sunset\nmove the palm trees apart; they overlap\nmake the island roughly 300 wide and 200 high\nset the compass rose to the top right of the map\nadd a dotted path from the beach to the jungle, a stream crossing it, a fallen log over the stream, and a parrot above the canopy\ncan you show me the drawing without the grid lines?\nwhere did my starfish go? bring it back to the rock\nhvae the boy wave at the girl on the bridge\ndraw a yurt with a round door facing the morning sun\nmake the campfire glow warm orange and add two logs crossed beneath it\nset tent canvas beige poles brown\nI wonder if the bear should be catching a fish mid stream\nnext to the tent put a backpack, a kettle, and a pair of boots\ntop the totem pole with a carved eagle\nthen make the totem three faces tall instead of two\nits supose to look cozy so warm the colors up a bit\ntell me what the tiny shape near the fence is\ncan you stretch the beach so it fills the bottom third\ndrop in a message in a bottle on the sand\nset message bottle green cork brown\nline the swans up so the middle one is furthest away\nagain remove the buoy this time\nwhat if the lighthouse beam swept to the left\nshow what changed after the color pass\ncould you please not touch the foreground; only fix the sky\nmake the picture 50% bigger but keep it centered\nput a wreath on the door, holly on the window sills, and lights strung along the eaves\nset wreath green bow red\nthanks, that is exactly what I meant!\nthen move the sleigh behind the fir trees\ndraw a hot air balloon, striped red and cream, drifting left of the mountains\nset balloon stripes red cream\nwhere is the basket of the balloon attached? lower it a touch\nthe chimney smoke curling right, the shutters half open, the cat watching from a sill — keep those details, just refine them\nmkae the snow drifts rounder\nhand the snowman a broom instead of a cane\nadd icicles under the north eave only\ncan you mirror the left cottage as a twin on the right\ninstead of a path make it a cobbled street with a lamp\nset street lamps glowing amber\nI wonder if you could thin out the crowd in the square\nnext erase the scaffolding on the clock tower\ntell me how the fountain will look once the water is added\ndrop in a pigeon near the fountain rim\nset pigeon gray beak orange\nmake the square big enough for the bandstand to breathe\nthen add bunting from the lamp posts to the bandstand\nhighest first: sort the roofs by height when you place them in the skyline\nwhere do the steps of the stairs land? show me\npleese make the cloumns of the veranda the same thickness\nset veranda white railings cream\ncould you put a rocking chair on the veranda facing the fields\nthat would help.\nmove the scarecrow's arm — just the left one; then leave it\nadd a fox slipping between the hedge and the shed, tail up, ears back\nset fox orange white chest\nwhat if the hedge ran all the way around the garden\nshow what changed to the hedge\nhvae the hen peck near the coop door\ndraw a trampoline with one kid mid bounce, socks flying, and a dog watching from the grass\nmake the trampoline round and about 80 across\ncan you tell me which object is nearest the viewer\ntell me which is nearest, then fix the overlaps so it stays that way\ninstead of a single tree make it an orchard, five rows deep\nset orchard rows green trunks brown\nthen a wheelbarrow of apples at the front edge\nI wonder if you could make the horizon lower\nmake the picture half its current size\nadd a mousehole at the base of the skirting board and a bit of cheese beside it\nset mousehole black arch small\nwhere is the cat now? it should be on the sofa\ndrop in a ball of yarn under the coffee table\nagain with the tail curled this time\ncan you shade the sofa so the room feels evening\nthe lamp on, the curtain drawn, the book open on the armrest — all of those, but softly\nthanks, perfect!\nnext put a rug under the sofa, oval, warm red\npleese make the cloumns of the bookshelf less wobbly\nline the books up on the second shelf\ntop the stack of books with a tiny plant\ntell me where the hallway light falls\nset window moonlight blue\nI wonder if you could add rain on the window, streaks only\nwhat if the cat sat on the windowsill instead\nshow what changed to the room scene\nmove the mouse — the computer kind; then zoom in\nhvae the pencil lean against the mug\ndraw a desk with a mug, a lamp, loose papers, and a monitor showing a small boat\nset monitor screen boat blue\ncan the lamp light come from the left? shade it that way\ninstead of papers scatter a few envelopes\nset envelopes cream wax seal red\nthen straighten the blotter\nmake the mug 8 wide and 10 high roughly\ntell me if the perspective of the desk looks off\ncould you tilt the monitor a few degrees toward the chair\nthat would help a lot.\nwhere should the cable run? hide it behind the desk\ndrop in a cat curled on the chair\nset cat curled gray tail wrapped\nagain, no whiskers this time\nadd a lighthouse beam sweeping the sea, a dinghy dodging it, and stars coming out above the cliff\nset beam pale yellow wide\npleese make the cloumns of light from the stars thin\nwhat if the dinghy had a small lantern\nshow what changed on the horizon\nthen fade the cliff edge into mist\ncan you make the mist stop before the waterline\nset mist white translucent\nI wonder if you could put a distant ferry on the left horizon\nthanks!\ninstead of mist make it low fog in bands\ndraw a castle gate with a portcullis, braziers either side, and a guard holding a long spear\nset portcullis iron gray\nhvae the guard face the bridge\nmake the braziers flicker with tiny sparks\ntell me where the drawbridge hinges should be\ntop the gatehouse with crenellations\nthen add a banner: blue, with a white fish, hanging from the middle merlon\nset banner blue white fish\nwhere does the moat reflect the torchlight? hint it a little\ncould you darken the moat water\nthat is all; save it\nnext move the whole gate left by 30\nmake the gate 100 wide and 90 high\nI wonder if a raven would fit on the roof\npleese make the cloumns of the arch wider at the base\ndrop in a frog on a lily pad by the moat edge\nset frog green eyes bulgy\nline the torches up along the causeway\nagain two more this time\nshow what changed after the torch pass\ncan you make the causeway stones uneven, like old work\nset stones gray moss green\nthanks, looks right now\n"
