    "title": "file_system.bash",
    "detail": {
      "toolName": "file_system.bash",
      "display": {
        "summary": "bash: cat >> /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-drawing.txt <<'CHUNK_EOF'\nadd a ferris wheel at the far end of the funfair, tents along the midway, a queue by the ticket booth, and bunting strung between the poles\nset ferris wheel spokes red cabins yellow\ncan you make the carousel horses move up and down\ntell me where the band is standing in this scene\npleese make the cloumns of the ticket booth taller\nhvae the clown juggle three rings\nmake the stage wide and shallow, roughly 240 by 90\ndraw a spotlight cone from the rig down to the singer\nset spotlight warm white translucent\nwhat if the curtains were parted in the middle instead of open wide\nthen add a microphone stand at the front of the stage\nagain, tilt it slightly\nwhere did the orchestra go? I wanted them behind the singer\ndrop in a cello leaning on a chair at the side\nset cello amber brown\nI wonder if you could scatter sheet music on the floor around the stands\nmake the chairs: four rows of five, facing the stage\nset chairs black legs chrome\ncould you darken the audience area so the stage pops\nthat would help.\nthanks a lot!\nline the music stands up in an arc\ninstead of chairs make the front two rows benches\nnext add a drum kit at the back, half hidden by a cymbal\nshow what changed behind the drums\nmove the piano — the grand one, not the keyboard; then close the lid\nset piano lid black gloss open\ncan you put a vase of lilies on the piano\ntell me which way the pianist faces\ntop the piano with sheet music, fanned\nthen draw a bow on the cello case\nits to blurry at the back edge, sharpen the stalls\nmkae the stage boards run side to side\nadd a penguin sliding on its belly, a second one waving from an ice floe, and a third asleep standing up\nset penguins black white beak orange\nwhat if the aurora rippled a little further south\nmake the igloo about 90 wide and 60 high\nset igloo snow blocks pale blue\ncould you add a fishing hole with a thin ice rim\ndrop in a lantern beside the hole\nagain make the lantern light warm this time\nI wonder if the sled dogs should be mid stride\ntell me where the sled runner lines bend\npleese make the cloumns of ice at the glacier face more jagged\nset glacier ice blue white streaks\nthen a polar bear sitting far left, tiny, for scale\nwhere does the horizon sit? I think it is too high\nhvae the pup nuzzle the musher's boot\nline the dogs up in pairs, lines taut\nshow what changed to the sky colors\ninstead of stars make it a pale green shimmer\nset aurora green violet ribbons\ncan you thin the aurora so the stars show through\nnext put a small flag on the nearest ice hummock\nthanks!\ndraw a greenhouse with trays of seedlings, a watering can on the bench, a pair of gloves draped over a pot, and tomatoes ripening on a vine\nset greenhouse glass pale tinted\nmake the greenhouse 150 wide and 110 high\ntop the tomato vine with a tie-back string\nset tomato vine green red fruit\nwhat if the seedling trays were staggered, not aligned\nthen mist the glass with a hint of condensation\nagain with the door ajar this time\ntell me where the sun falls inside the greenhouse\nhvae the gardener kneel by the second bench\ncould you put a bucket under the leaky tap\ndrop in a ladybird on the nearest leaf\nset ladybird red spots black\nI wonder if the gardener needs a hat\npleese make the cloumns of the staging slats even\nmake the hose coil into a loose spiral by the door\nset hose green nozzle brass\nwhere is the spade? I asked for it by the door\nline the pots up on the shelf, smallest to largest\nthen add a seed packet leaning against the pots\nset seed packet cream illustration tomato\ninstead of tomatoes on the vine put peppers\nshow what changed on the back bench\ncan you shade the path outside gravel gray\nthat would help.\nnext a wheelbarrow outside the door, slightly tipped\nmkae the compost bin less round\ndraw an allotment: five beds, a shed at the top, canes tied in a teepee, and a sunflower leaning badly\nset sunflower yellow petals brown center\ntell me if the teepee canes cross anywhere\ncould you tie the leaning sunflower to a cane\ndrop in a bee near the sunflower head\nagain two more bees further off\nhvae the scarecrow face the pigeons\nwhat if the beds were numbered with little signs\nset bed signs wood lettering white\nthen thin the carrot tops, they are crowded\npleese make the cloumns of the beanpoles straighter\nwhere should the wheelbarrow go so it blocks nothing\nthanks, lovely!\ninstead of a shed put a cold frame\nset cold frame glass lid propped\nline the onions up in a drying rack row\ntop the shed roof with a weathervane rooster\nmake the rooster small, maybe 15 tall\nI wonder if you could add a cat asleep on the cold frame\nthen show me the allotment at dusk\nset dusk sky peach lavender\ncan you turn the porch light on in the shed\ntell me what still needs drawing in this scene\nmove the spade — the one in the shed; then lock up\nthat is all for now.\nadd a unicorn by the stream, a fairy on a toadstool, a dragonfly above the reeds, and a rainbow starting behind the willow\nset unicorn white mane rainbow\nmake the willow trail its branches into the water\nset willow trunk gnarled green canopy\nwhat if the fairy had glowing wings\nthen sprinkle tiny lights between the trees\nagain fewer lights this time, it is not a city\npleese make the cloumns of the toadstools thinner\ndrop in a snail on the nearest toadstool cap\nset snail shell spiral brown\ntell me where the stream exits the picture\nhvae the dragonfly hover over the fairy\ncould you bend the rainbow a little tighter\nmake the stream 40 wide at the bottom, narrowing to 10 at the top\nset stream blue sparkles white\nI wonder if the moss should creep up the willow\nwhere is the magic coming from? maybe a hint of glow at the fairy\nline the pebbles up along the near bank\ninstead of pebbles make it fine gravel\nthen a fox watching from the ferns, only ears and eyes showing\nshow what changed in the glade\nnext soften the edges of everything mid distance\ncan you make the toadstools red with white spots again\nset toadstools red spots white\nthanks, that reads better!\nmkae the ferns less pointy\nadd a harbor with trawlers in, a crane on the quay, coils of rope, fish crates stacked, and gulls arguing over a scrap\nset trawlers green hull white superstructure\ntell me which boat is the biggest\nmake the crane arm reach over the water\nset crane yellow warn stripes\nwhat if the fish crates were blue, not gray\npleese make the cloumns of crates stack properly\ndrop in a cat between the crates\nagain make the cat ginger this time\nhvae the crane hook sway a little to the right\ncould you add a forklift near the warehouse door\nset forklift orange black wheels\nthen a queue of lorries along the top of the quay\nmake the warehouse 400 wide and 120 high\nset warehouse gray roof rust\nI wonder if the tide should be low, with mud showing\ntell me where the quay edge is so the boats do not sit on it\nline the bollards up along the quay wall\ninstead of bollards make them mooring rings\nthen add a life ring on the warehouse wall\nset life ring orange white rope\nshow what changed to the moorings\nnext darken the water under the boats\ncan you reflect the crane in the wet quay\nwhere do the lobster pots go? stack them near the rope\npleese make the cloumns of the jetty piles stand straight\nthat would help.\nthanks, spot on!\ndraw a jungle ruin with vines over the doorway, a monkey on a broken column, a parrot in the sunlight, and a snake shadow on the wall\nset vines dark green layered\nmake the doorway half collapsed on the left only\nset doorway stone gray moss green\nwhat if sunlight cut through the canopy in one shaft\nthen add dust motes in the light shaft\nset dust motes pale gold tiny\nagain make the shaft slant more to the left this time\nhvae the monkey hold a stolen mango\ncould you carve a faint glyph pattern on the lintel\nset glyphs weathered barely visible\ndrop in a butterfly above the monkey's head\nI wonder if the snake should actually show, tail only\ntell me where the explorer's path enters the scene\nmake the fallen column three chunks long\nset chunks stone ferns green\nline the roots up creeping down the wall\nthen soften the background into green haze\npleese make the cloumns of the colonnade mossy not clean\nwhere is the map marker in all this? the stone with the spiral\nshow what changed since the vines grew\ninstead of a monkey make it a toucan on the column\nset toucan black chest yellow beak huge\ncan you make the whole scene slightly cooler in tone\nthanks!\nnext undo the cool tone, keep everything else\nmake it: a whale tail far out, a sailboat nearer, a buoy rocking in the swell, and gannets diving\nset whale tail dark slate wet shine\ntell me how far out the whale is supposed to be\nmake the swell gentle, no whitecaps near the boat\nset sailboat tan sail white\nwhat if the buoy had a stripe\ndrop in a reflection line under the whale tail\nagain a shorter reflection this time\ncould you put the sun low behind the whale\npleese make the cloumns of light on the water shimmer\nset sun path gold on water\nI wonder if the gannets should be mid dive, folded\nthen add a distant headland on the right horizon\nset headland blue gray misty\nline the waves up so they all travel the same way\ninstead of gannets make them gulls\nshow what changed on the waterline\nnext add a small child's bucket on the shore, foreground\nset bucket red spade yellow\nwhere should the wet sand band end? blend it\nthat is everything, thanks!\nmove the whale tail right by 20 and make it smaller; then check it does not clash with the sailboat\nmkae the swell lines thinner toward the horizon\nset horizon line faint blue\nadd a village well with a bucket on a rope, a woman drawing water, ducks in a puddle, and laundry strung between cottages\nset well stone gray roof tiled\nhvae the woman brace against the rope\nCHUNK_EOF\nwc -l /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-drawing.txt",
        "content": null,
        "suffix": "",
