    "type": "reasoning",
    "text": "Drawing done: 600 lines, 0 duplicates. Now diagram file. Mark todo. Write chunk 1 (200 lines) via write_file, then appends. This time I'll count carefully — the earlier issue was that my \"200\" chunks were off. I'll count in exact groups of 10 as I compose.\n\nDiagram vocabulary: nodes, boxes, arrows, edges, labels, lanes, layers, clusters, align, distribute, group, ungroup, snap to grid, legend, title, caption, flowchart, sequence, org chart, network topology, ER diagram, gantt, bar chart, axis ranges (10^1 to 10^6), log scale, tick spacing, series, dashed lines, bidirectional arrows, ortho routing, colors, sizes (x 120 y 40), \"line Stove and Fridge up\", \"top the tower\"? For diagram: \"top the tallest bar with its value\".\n\nNames: Stove, Fridge, Server, Backup, Router, Gateway, Auth, Cache, Queue, Worker, DB, API, Client, Browser, CDN, Load balancer, Sensor, Motor, Pump, Valve, Boiler, Tank, Filter, Heater, Thermostat, Meter, Alarm, Robot, Conveyor, Press, Crane, Warehouse, Order, Payment, Invoice, Cart, Stock, Shipment.\n\nConstructions same 8 categories. \"line Stove and Fridge up\" is cat 6 for diagram. Other noun/verb lookalikes: \"top the tallest bar with its value\", \"table the...\" hmm. \"left the label\"? \"center the title\", \"justify\"? \"chart the chart\"? \"graph the growth\", \"flow the flow\"? \"queue the Queue node\"? \"route the Router to the edge\"? \"back up Backup\"? \"drop in a Sink node\", \"level the baseline\", \"water?\" no. \"letter the nodes A to F\" (letter as verb). \"number the states 1 to 6\" (number as verb). \"face the arrows downward\". \"head the diagram with a title\" (head as verb). \"foot the diagram with a caption\"? \"foot the table\". \"bracket the group\". \"dash the edge\" hmm. \"curve the Curve node\"? \"scale the y axis 10^1 to 10^6\" (scale as verb). \"point the pointer at Queue\". \"state the states\"? \"event the events\"? \"stack the Stack\". \"frame the frame\". \"circle the circle\"? good: \"circle the node called Gate\" — draw a circle around. \"box the label\"? \"arrow the connection\"? no.\n\nTypos for diagram: \"algin\", \"alight\"? \"mkae the arwos solid\", \"set teh edge dashd\", \"hvae the arrows point left\", \"pleese make the coloumns of boxes even\", \"recieve\"? \"definately\", \"seperate the clusters\", \"shwo what changed\", \"conect\", \"delet\", \"mov\", \"nad\", \"teh\".\n\nMissing words: \"connect Server DB\", \"move label left\", \"add node top right\", \"make edge dashed blue\", \"delete cluster 2\".\n\nMeasures: \"make it 160 wide and 100 high\", \"four blocks wide and five blocks tall\", \"x 120 y 40\", \"10^1 to 10^6\", \"gap 20\", \"radius 30\", \"80 by 60\".\n\nLong lists after participle: \"put the pipeline left to right: Sensor feeding the Meter, the Meter feeding the Alarm, the Alarm wired to the Panel, and the Panel reporting to the Cloud\" — participial phrases: \"a sensor reading temperature, a meter logging the flow, an alarm waiting on the threshold, all feeding into the panel\".\n\nOK compose 200 lines exactly, 20 groups of 10. Let me write.",
