    "relatedEntryId": null,
    "type": "effect",
    "title": "file_system.write_file",
    "detail": {
      "toolName": "file_system.write_file",
      "display": {
        "summary": "Writing generated-diagram.txt",
        "content": "connect Server to Backup with a dashed arrow\nline Stove and Fridge up so their tops are level\npleese make the cloumns of boxes the same width\nset node Backup brown large\ntell me where the Queue node ended up\nthen move Auth under the Gateway\nmake the canvas 160 wide and 100 high\ncan you show what changed after the relayout\nwhat if you grouped the payment boxes together — try that\nadd a sensor reading temperature, a meter logging the flow, an alarm waiting on the threshold, and a panel wired to all three\ncould you label the edge between Router and Switch\nhighest first: sort the bars by value and relabel the axis\nx 120 y 40 for the API node\nhvae the arrows point left to right\ninstead of a solid line make the payment edge dashed\nnext add a swim lane for finance\nshow what changed\nI wonder if you could make the cluster border rounded\ndrop in a note above the Boiler node\nthat would help.\nthanks a lot!\nmake the flowchart four blocks wide and five blocks tall\nset node Router blue square\nremove the second arrow; the first one can stay\nwhere is the legend? I asked for one bottom right\nthen add a title above everything: Order pipeline, v2\ncan you connect Client, Gateway, Auth and Cache in a chain\ntell me which edges cross each other\nmkae the arrowheads smaller\nagain, run the layout left to right this time\nset edge Queue Worker gray dashed\ndraw a diamond after the Review box and route both branches out of it\nset diamond decision yellow\nwhat if the retry loop went back to the start instead of to step three\nscale the y axis from 10^1 to 10^6\nthen use a log grid with light lines\ncould you put tick labels at every power of ten\nset axis labels 9 point gray\nI wonder if the bars should be sorted or stay in date order\nhighest first, please, and drop the smallest one\nline the bars up on the baseline, no gaps of zero\ntop the tallest bar with its value\npleese make the cloumns of the chart narrower\nthanks, that reads much better!\nmove the legend — the one inside the plot; then shrink it\nset legend frame none\nwhere did the second series go? bring it back in orange\ninstead of two series make it one with a moving average line\nshow what changed in the top right corner\nnext put a caption under the chart: monthly signups\nset caption 10 point italic\nthat is all; save it\nalgin the boxes on the grid, they look hand placed\nhvae the Server node face the traffic arrow\ndrop in a boundary box around the whole internal network\nset boundary dashed blue label internal\nwhat if the boundary hugged the nodes tightly\nthen add a pad of 20 around it\nagain no fill this time, just the dashed border\ntell me where the labels overlap the edges\ncould you reroute the edge from Boiler to Pump around the Tank\nset edge Boiler Pump solid red 2pt\nline the pumps up along the bottom wall\ninstead of arrows use plain lines with small squares\nmake the Tank 80 by 60 and the Pipes 4 thick\nset Tank label bold\nI wonder if the pipes should curve instead of elbowing\npleese make the cloumns of the node grid line up\nshow what changed after snapping\nthanks!\nnext up: the org chart needs a second level under the CEO\nset CEO node gold rounded\ncan you hang three managers off the CEO: Sales, Ops, Tech\ntell me how deep the tree is now\nhvae the Tech manager branch spread wider than the others\nmove the tree — the whole subtree under Ops; then rebalance\nset subtree spacing 40 vertical 25\nwhat if the connector lines were orthogonal instead of curved\nthen add little elbow guides at each turn\nagain keep the root centered this time\ndrop in a floating note: pending reorg, do not publish\nset note yellow sticky small\nwhere should the assistants go? hang two off Sales\nline the leaf nodes up in one row at the bottom\nthat would help.\nmkae the connectors thinner, they shout\ninstead of a chart make it a radial mind map\nshow what changed since the last layout\nthanks, much cleaner!\ndefinately seperate the two clusters, they overlap badly\nconnect Stove, Fridge, Meter and Panel in a ring\nset ring edges bidirectional\ncan you tell me which node has the most connections\nhighest first: order the nodes by degree and list them in the console\nthen color the top three nodes red, orange, yellow\nset colors red orange yellow graduated\nI wonder if isolated nodes should move to a side panel\ndrop the unused nodes in the corner; label them orphaned\nset orphan label gray italic\nwhat if I told you the Meter was deprecated — remove it and rewire\nshow what changed to the ring\nnext check that every node still has a label\npleese make the cloumns of the dashboard widgets even\nx 120 y 40 for the small gauge, width 60 height 60\nset gauge needle red arc green\ncould you add a threshold line at 80 percent\nset threshold amber dashed thick\ntell me where the gauge reads now\nhvae the gauge sweep clockwise from the left\nagain make the arc a full circle this time\ninstead of a gauge make it a small sparkline\nset sparkline blue dots none\nthanks, perfect!\nadd a state machine: Idle, Heating, Ready, Fault, with the arrows showing legal jumps\nset state circles gray borders 2\nmake the Fault state red with a double border\nset Fault label white bold\nwhat if the Reset arrow went back to Idle directly\nthen loop Heating to itself with a retry label\nset self loop label retry x3\nshow what changed in the state diagram\ntell me which states are unreachable\ncould you list them for me, highest count first\npleese make the cloumns of the text in the boxes wider\nline the state circles up in two neat rows\nnext move Fault to the far right corner\nagain with a bigger gap this time\nmkae the transitions arc a little more\nwhere does the entry arrow come from? the left, I think\nset entry arrow green\ndrop in an initial dot before Idle\nthat would help a lot.\nthanks!\nconnect Router to Switch, Switch to Hub, Hub to every machine\nset Router icon blue\ncan you make the Hub the center of a star instead\ntell me which machine is furthest from the Router\nwhat if the wifi nodes floated above the wired ones\nthen add a wavy radio link from Router to Laptop\nset radio link dotted teal\nagain with two arcs for signal strength\npleese make the cloumns of the rack diagram match the real rack\nset rack units numbered 1 to 42\nline the rack units up bottom to top, heaviest at the bottom\ninstead of numbering label each unit with its hostname\nshow what changed in the rack view\nnext add a cable tray above the rack, a simple gray channel\nset cable tray gray wide\nI wonder if the power feeds should be a separate layer\nthanks, looks legit!\nhvae the firewall block the direct path from Laptop to DB\ndraw a detour around the firewall through the proxy\nset proxy path orange\nmake it clear the proxy is the only allowed route\ntell me where the blocked path was removed from\ncould you stamp a small padlock on the firewall icon\nset padlock gold small\nwhat if the whole DMZ got a pale wash behind it\nset DMZ wash 10 percent blue\nnext up, add three clients below the LB with even fan out\nset LB node purple hexagon\nline the three clients up with a gap of 30\nshow what changed to the fan\ninstead of three clients show five, same gap\nthanks, exactly the shape I meant!\nthat would help a lot.\npleese make the cloumns of the matrix cells equal width\nset matrix rows 5 cols 5\ncan you shade the cell at row 2 col 3 light green\ntell me which cells are still empty\nwhat if the header row got a darker tone\nthen bold the header labels\nset header fill charcoal white text\nagain center the header text this time\ndrop in row numbers down the left side\nset row numbers gray right aligned\nI wonder if the cells should be square\nmake the cells 40 by 40 with 4 gap\nline the matrix up centered under its title\nnext label the top axis months and the left axis products\nshow what changed to the grid\nthanks!\nmkae the tick font smaller, it is cramped\nwhere is the title of the matrix? add one bold above\ninstead of months use weeks 1 to 5\nset week labels rotated 45\nthat is the matrix sorted; save it\nhvae the Kanban columns pull their titles from the labels\nadd four columns: backlog, doing, review, done\nset column widths equal\ncan you move the top card from doing to review\nthen move the rest down to fill the gap\nagain no animation preview this time, just do it\ntell me which column is tallest\nhighest first: order the cards in backlog by priority\nset card colors by priority red to green\ndrop in a blocked tag on the third card\nset blocked tag red flag icon\nwhat if the done column collapsed to a slim strip\nshow what changed on the board\nnext add a wip limit note above doing\nset wip note 3 max amber\npleese make the cloumns of cards the same height\nline the cards up with a small overlap like a deck\nthanks, tidy!\nI wonder if the swim lanes should be horizontal after all\ninstead of vertical lanes rotate the whole board\nmake the lanes four blocks wide and five blocks tall each\nset lane titles bold vertical\ncould you shade alternate lanes very light gray\nset lane shade 5 percent\nthat would help the eye.\nmkae the lane separators fainter\nwhere does the footer note go? pin it bottom left\nset footer note 8 point gray\ndrop in an arrow from the blocked card to the wip note\nagain a curved arrow this time\nshow what changed since the tag was added\nnext hide the done column completely\nthanks, that clears it up!\nletter the milestones A to F along the timeline\nset milestone diamonds dark blue\ncan you stretch the timeline so the gap from B to C is honest\ntell me where today should sit on the line\nwhat if the phases floated above as bands\nset phase bands pastel thin\nthen label the bands early, build, launch\nagain thicken the bands this time\nline the milestones up on the axis, diamonds on the marks\ninstead of diamonds use flags\nshow what changed along the axis\nnext add a red today line, dashed, full height\nset today line red dashed\npleese make the cloumns of the phase table match the bands\nI wonder if the first milestone should be a circle instead\nmkae the date labels smaller under the marks\nthanks!\nwhere does the axis start? pull it back to January\nset axis start January end December\nthat is the plan; save it.\n",
