        "message": "cat >> /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-diagram.txt <<'CHUNK_EOF'\ndraw the four C4 layers for the booking system, one layer per page\nset level one context center system\ncan you add the person actor on the left of the context page\ntell me which container talks to the payment provider\nwhat if the database sat in its own boundary\nthen label the boundary booking persistence\nset boundary label small navy\nagain with the boundary dashed this time\ndrop in a data flow arrow labeled booking xml\nset data flow label italic tiny\nline the containers up left to right by responsibility\ninstead of four pages make it one page, four stacked bands\nshow what changed since the split\nnext shrink the container boxes so the arrows fit\npleese make the cloumns of band titles bold and even\nI wonder if the actor should be named customer or guest\nmkae the provider a gray box, outside our system\nwhere does the legend of arrow types go? last page, bottom\nset arrow legend solid dashed dotted\nthanks, architecture in one glance!\nthat would help the review.\nchart the weekly totals as bars, seven bars only\nset bars sky blue baseline zero\ncan you top each bar with its own number\ntell me which week dipped\nwhat if weeks without data showed a faint outline bar\nthen gray out the two holidays\nset holiday markers gray flags\nagain no flags this time, just gray bars\ndrop in a moving average line over the bars\nset average line dark blue smooth\nline the weekday labels up under their bars\ninstead of seven days show only weekdays\nshow what changed at the right edge\nnext put the unit in the axis label, not each bar\nset axis label signups per week\npleese make the cloumns of the axis ticks align right\nI wonder if a stacked split by source would read better\nmkae the stack gap 1, they should touch\nwhere should the source names go? legend on the right\nset source legend right stacked\nthanks, the dip is obvious now!\nhvae the burndown chart start at 120 points\nset ideal line gray dashed straight\ncan you plot the actual as a jagged teal line\nthen circle the sprint where it went flat\nset sprint circle red thin\nwhat if the flat sprint got a note\nset flat note retrospective spike\nagain keep the note tiny this time\ndrop in the remaining axis on the right too\nset right axis points remaining\ntell me where the velocity line crosses the ideal\nline the sprint labels up along the bottom\ninstead of jagged smooth the actual line slightly\nshow what changed in the last three sprints\nnext shade the region between actual and ideal\nset region shade 10 percent teal\npleese make the cloumns of the sprint table below match the chart\nI wonder if weekends belong on the burndown\nmkae the chart area wider, 500 by 260\nwhere does the team name go? title, left side\nset team name title bold left\nthanks, scrum master approved!\ntable the second proposal in the appendix as a matrix\ngraph the error rate per release as small dots\nstack the layers of the protocol on the left\nscale the x axis 10^1 to 10^6 and tell me if it still reads\nframe the caption in a hairline box\nset caption frame hairline\nalot of edges cross near the middle; untangle them\nseperate the legend from the plot area, it overlaps now\nrecieve no updates from the source, so freeze the chart as is\nwich node is the bottleneck? tell me before I decide\nthier labels drifted, pin them to the boxes again\nits to wide, the diagram spills past the margin\nmkae teh gap between clusters at least 40\nmov the label Backup above its box\nconnect Server DB directly, forget the gateway for now\nadd node top right corner small red\nset label bold dark\nhvae the arrows bend around the new node\npleese make the cloumns line up, i keep saying it\nline the ports up on the left edge of the chassis block\ntop the tower of stacked icons with a little flag\ndrop in an umbrella group over the whole rainy day scenario\nset umbrella dashed navy translucent\nwhat if the umbrella only covered the outdoor nodes\nagain lift it 10 so it clears the labels\ntell me where the outdoor nodes begin and end\nI wonder if a caption under the group would help instead\nshow what changed since the umbrella went up\nnext fold the umbrella away, keep the dashed outline\nset outline navy 1pt dashed\nthanks, much tidier!\ncould you check the diagram reads okay at half size\nthen export half size and show me\nthat is the last change; thanks!\nCHUNK_EOF\nwc -l /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-diagram.txt && sort /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-diagram.txt | uniq -d",
