  {
    "id": "reasoning-57c85dbb-f38c-58e6-b0ab-fe98ec7aed72-0",
    "sessionId": "b6e04fad-5ad6-a68d-a9a4-f7c44605cea2",
    "turnId": "turn-7b80f7c1e80ca6211089f92ed8b4eb00",
    "inputEntryId": "user-turn-7b80f7c1e80ca6211089f92ed8b4eb00-1",
    "createdAt": 1795861162244,
    "updatedAt": 1795861162244,
    "generationStatus": "completed",
    "relatedEntryId": null,
    "type": "reasoning",
    "text": "Diagram done: 600, 0 duplicates. Now calendar. Mark todo, write chunk 1.\n\nCalendar vocabulary: events, meetings, invites, attendees, recurring, reminders, all-day, timezones, rooms, calendars (work, personal, family, gym), focus blocks, PTO, holidays, birthdays, deadlines, sync, color coding, sharing, permissions, tentative, conflict, double booking, reschedule, push, move up, duration, buffer, travel time, attachments, agenda, minutes, standup, retro, planning, 1:1, skip-level, all-hands, on-call rotation, dentist, doctor, haircut, dinner, movie, concert, school pickup, swim class, book club.\n\nConstructions same. Noun/verb lookalikes: \"book the book club room\" (book as verb + book club noun!), \"mark the calendar\" (mark), \"table the...\" no. \"calendar the event\"? weird. Good ones: \"book the book club slot\", \"face the...\"? \"head the week with a planning block\" (head as verb), \"top the week off with drinks on Friday\" (top off), \"hand the...\"? \"drop in a dentist appointment\" (drop in), \"line the...\"? \"level the workload across the week\", \"flag the double booking\", \"shield the afternoon\" (shield as verb! like \"shield the afternoon from meetings\"), \"guard Friday morning\"? \"reserve\", \"block the block\"? \"schedule the schedule\"? \"table the Tuesday conflict\"? \"present\"? \"park the...\"? \"second the...\"? \"minute the minutes\"? \"date the date change\"? \"calendar the calendar\"? — \"set calendar Family green\" is cat 8. \"leave the leaves\"? no. \"spring the clocks forward\", \"fall the clocks back\"! Nice: \"spring the clocks forward an hour\" / \"fall the clocks back\". \"watch the watch party\"? \"party the...\"? \"back the back-to-back...\"? \"water\"? \"plant a recurring reminder\" (plant as verb), \"shower\"? Let me use: book the book club, spring the clocks, fall the clocks back, head the week, top the week off, shield the afternoons, flag the clash, level the load, plant a reminder, drop in a hold, minute? \"time the reminder\" (time as verb!), \"mark the marketing review\" (mark + marketing), \"table the...\"? \"count the countdown\"? \"date night the calendar\"? enough.\n\nMeasures for calendar: \"make the block 90 minutes\", \"from 10^1 to...\"? no. \"x 120 y 40\" fits grid position? For calendar maybe \"zoom to 15 minute rows\" or \"set the week grid 7 columns\". \"10^1 to 10^6\" was a chart thing; for calendar could be a weird scale ask? Keep measures as durations/sizes: \"make the buffer 15 minutes\", \"the room fits 12\", \"set week view five days wide\", \"three rows tall\"? I'll do \"show the week view, days 100 wide and header 40 high\"? plausible for a calendar layout assistant. Also \"x 120 y 40\" could be a position of a floating widget. Fine.\n\nTypos: \"tommorow\", \"tueday\", \"wendsday\", \"thusrday\", \"definately\", \"shedule\", \"calender\", \"occured\", \"recieve\", \"cancellation\" as \"cancelation\", \"pls\", \"its at 3 i think\", \"hvae the meeting start at 9\", \"mov my dentist to friday\", \"book room 4 for the standup\".\n\nMissing words: \"move standup 9\", \"set event weekly Tuesday\", \"add lunch noon\", \"delete the 3pm\", \"push retro one hour later\"? that's fine actually. Missing: \"invite Ana Ben\", \"make recurring every Monday\", \"change title bold\"? etc.\n\nLong lists after participle: \"clear my Friday: the sync with Ana, the design review, the two standups, and the hold someone put at noon\" and participial: \"a week with back to back calls, three birthday lunches queued, a dentist visit hiding mid Tuesday, and a deadline looming Friday\".\n\nOrder/time words: \"earliest first\", \"chronological, newest first\", \"highest priority first\", \"then\", \"next\", \"instead\", \"again\", \"this time\".\n\nEmbedded questions: \"tell me when the retro is\", \"show what changed on my week\", \"can you find a slot Thursday morning?\", \"what if we moved planning to Wednesday\", \"I wonder if Friday afternoon is free\".\n\nNames/values: \"set event standup 9am daily\", \"set calendar Work blue\", \"set event Dentist 14:30 recurring none\", \"set reminder 15 min before\", \"heading...\"? no that's document. For calendar: \"set block Deep work 2h green\", \"set room Atlantis capacity 8\", \"set invite Ana optional\".\n\nWrite chunk 1 (~200 lines; I'll aim 200 exactly but will verify with wc and correct after). Let me carefully write 20 groups of 10.",
