    "type": "reasoning",
    "text": "192 lines. Need 408 more, in 2-3 chunks. Let me append chunk 2 of about 200 lines (20 groups of 10), then chunk 3 to fill the remainder.\n\nMore calendar themes: interviews, client calls, travel/flights, hotels, conferences, PTO/vacation, sick leave, on-call, shift rota, school events, sports fixtures, reminders vs events, tentative events, recurring edge cases (last Friday of month, every 3rd Wednesday, every other week), timezones, DST (\"spring the clocks forward\"), swap shifts, delegate, permissions/sharing, agenda templates, meeting minutes links, attachments, RSVPs, waitlist, cancellation policy, buffer defaults, focus time auto-scheduling, working hours, multiple calendars overlay, availability sharing, find-a-time, rescheduling chains, snooze, \"hold vs confirmed\", deadlines vs events, all-day banners, week numbering, fiscal quarters, sprint boundaries.\n\nCat 6 noun/verb: \"book the book...\", \"spring the clocks forward an hour\", \"fall the clocks back\", \"head the week with a planning block\", \"top the week off with drinks Friday\", \"shield\", \"flag the clash\", \"level the load\", \"plant a reminder\", \"time the reminder for 8\", \"mark the marketing review\", \"table the...\" — \"table the discussion about the rota\" hmm, could keep. \"date the...\"? \"second the proposal in the notes\"? \"watch the watch party on Sunday\" — good. \"present\"? \"charge the...\"? no. \"face\"? \"time\" is great: \"time the reminder for 15 minutes before\". \"clock\" as verb: \"clock me out at 5\". \n\nWrite chunk 2 with ~200 lines.",
