        "message": "cat >> /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-calendar.txt <<'CHUNK_EOF'\ntable the rota discussion for the next all hands, we are out of time\nset rota discussion agenda item all hands\ncan you book the conference days off as PTO, the 12th to the 15th\nset PTO 12 to 15 all day teal recurring none\ntell me if my token balance covers four days\nwhat if I only took three and worked the Monday from there\nthen set PTO 13 to 15 and a remote block on the 12th\nagain full four days this time, I earned them\ndrop in a handover note the day before I leave\nset handover note 11th 4pm 60 minutes\nline the handover tasks up in a checklist in the description\ninstead of a checklist attach the runbook\nshow what changed to my last week in the office\nnext set an out of office reply spanning the whole block\nset OOO reply 12 to 15 polite bounce\npleese make the cloumns of the PTO balance widget smaller\nI wonder if sick leave should live in the same view\nmkae sick leave appear only for me and my manager\nthanks, time off handled!\nthat would help the team plan around me.\nclock me out at 5, add a stop event on my focus block\nset stop event 5pm daily silent\ncan you tally my meeting hours per week in the corner\nthen compare against last quarter, tiny bar chart is fine\nset meeting tally corner chart week vs quarter\nagain no chart this time, just the number\ntell me which week was the worst for meetings\nhighest first: rank the last eight weeks by meeting load\nline the tally up under the mini month in the sidebar\ninstead of hours show it as a percentage of work time\nshow what changed to the sidebar stats\nnext warn me if a week will exceed 40 percent meetings\nset meeting load warning 40 percent amber\npleese make the cloumns of the stats block line up\nI wonder if focus hours should sit next to meeting hours\nmkae both numbers the same size, meeting and focus\nthanks, honest numbers at last!\nhvae the client calls all sit in the afternoon, my mornings are for work\nset client calls allowed 13:00 to 18:00 only\ncan you batch the three vendor calls on one afternoon\nthen space them 30 minutes apart with breaks\nset vendor calls Wednesday 2, 3, 4 spacing 30\nagain 2, 3:30, 5 this time, longer gaps\ntell me which vendor is in the wrong timezone for that slot\ndrop in a prep note 20 minutes before each call\nset prep note 20 minutes lavender auto\nline the call titles up consistently, vendor first then topic\ninstead of topic first make vendor first, clearer\nshow what changed to Wednesday afternoon\nnext cap client calls at four per week, decline the fifth politely\nset client cap 4 weekly polite message\nI wonder if the cap counts internal client team syncs\nmkae it count everything tagged client\nthanks, batched and bounded!\ncould you find a time when all five interviewers are free next week\nthen hold three candidate slots in the best window\nset candidate slots 60 minutes spaced 30 apart\nwhat if one interviewer is only free mornings\nthen keep the slots before noon, all three\nagain relax to 11 to 4 this time\ntell me who conflicts most, so I can swap them out\nhighest first: list the interviewers by conflict count\nline the panel assignments up so no one has back to back panels\ninstead of swapping remove the busiest panelist\nshow what changed to the interview day\nnext add a debrief 15 minutes after each slot\nset debrief 15 minutes auto panel only\npleese make the cloumns of the scorecard link in each invite even\nI wonder if candidates should see each other's slots, obviously not\nmkae candidate slots private by default, no exceptions\nthanks, hiring day is a machine now!\nthat would help the recruiters.\nmove the deadline: report due the 20th, not the 18th\nset report due 20th 5pm red flag\ncan you walk the dependent tasks forward two days too\nthen check the review still fits before the deadline\nagain pull the review earlier, not later, if it clashes\ntell me the new critical path for the report\nhighest first: order the subtasks by how much slack they lose\nline the subtasks up under the deadline flag in the sidebar\ninstead of the sidebar show them as a mini timeline\nshow what changed to the deadline view\nnext add a soft warning two days before every hard deadline\nset soft warning 2 days amber auto\nI wonder if deadlines should also block focus time for writing\nmkae the day before each deadline a writing day, protected\nthanks, deadlines with respect built in!\nhvae my availability link only show busy or free, no titles\nset availability link busy free only\ncan you regenerate the link for the hiring panel only\nthen expire the old one quietly\nset availability link hiring panel expires Friday\nagain no expiry this time, I trust them\ntell me who has used the link so far this week\ndrop in a booking page note: use the link, not my inbox\nset booking page note top banner small\nline the booking slots up on the half hour only\ninstead of half hours offer hourly slots, fewer no shows\nshow what changed to my bookable hours\nnext cap the booking page at three slots per day\nset booking cap 3 per day\npleese make the cloumns of the booking page match the brand colors\nI wonder if the page should show my timezone first\nmkae the visitor timezone the default, mine second\nthanks, scheduling self service!\nset event Portfolio review 10am 45 minutes recurring monthly\nflag the clash between the review and the offsite prep\ncan you move whichever one is easier to move\nthen tell the other attendees what changed and why\nagain no notification this time, I will talk to them\ntell me which recurrence rule handles the fifth Thursday\nhighest first: list the odd recurrences by how often they bite\nline the edge cases up in a test calendar so I can inspect\ninstead of a test calendar just annotate the real ones\nshow what changed to the recurring rules\nnext fix the every fifth Thursday rule, skip those months\nset rule fifth Thursday skip if absent\nI wonder if every other week even means the same to everyone\nmkae biweekly explicit: every 14 days, anchored Monday\nthanks, recurrences under control!\nthat would help end the arguments.\nset event Retro 4pm 90 minutes recurring per sprint\ncan you shrink the retro when the sprint is a short one\nthen keep the last Friday free no matter what\nset last Friday protected no exceptions\nagain allow only the all hands on last Fridays this time\ntell me how many ceremonies a normal sprint carries\nline the sprint template up so new sprints copy it\ninstead of copying ask me each time\nshow what changed to the sprint template\nnext add a wildcard slot every sprint for surprises\nset wildcard 60 minutes floating amber\nI wonder if the wildcard should be morning or afternoon\nmkae it afternoon, mornings are already spoken for\nthanks, the sprint breathes!\ncould you show the quarter as one long row, months on top\nset quarter view horizontal months labeled\ncan you put the fiscal quarters in a different shade than calendar ones\nthen label Q1 where the finance team thinks it starts\nset fiscal Q1 shade amber labeled\nagain calendar quarters on top, fiscal below this time\ntell me where the fiscal year actually starts here\ndrop in the board dates as small flags across the quarter\nset board flags navy small\nline the quarter boundaries up with the sprint lines\ninstead of thin lines use subtle column washes\nshow what changed to the quarter strip\nnext pin the two big launches as red diamonds on the strip\nset launch diamonds red labeled\npleese make the cloumns of the quarter strip equal, they wobble\nI wonder if holidays from three countries can overlay at once\nmkae UK and German holidays both show, tiny icons\nthanks, the year on one line!\nhvae the RSVP list show in the invite, not behind a click\nset RSVP list inline visible collapsed by default\ncan you chase the six who never answered\nthen chase only the externals, internals I will nag myself\nset chase externals polite 24 hours before\nagain no chase for the execs this time, I will do it\ntell me who declined without a reason, politely, privately\ndrop in a quorum note: do not meet if fewer than four accept\nset quorum rule 4 accepted\nline the attendees up: required first, optional grayed\ninstead of optional grayed make them italic\nshow what changed to the invite layout\nnext attach the agenda template to every recurring meeting\nset agenda template attach auto prefill\nI wonder if an empty agenda should cancel the meeting\nmkae meetings with empty agendas auto propose a skip\nthanks, fewer zombie meetings!\nthat would help everybody, honestly.\nmkae teh invite title say demo not demons, fix the typo\npleese fix the cloumns of the event editor, the time fields are misaligned\nits showing teh wrong week, refresh and check\ntommorow i mean the day after the holiday, account for it\nwendsday thursday whichever is free, book the review\nshedule the eye test whenever the optometrist has a slot\ncalender sync is off, my phone shows old events, investigate\ntueday morning i am driving, block it\nits at 3 i said, not 2, undo the change\nhvae the reminder fire twice, five and two minutes before\nmov the whole week forward one day, I lost my Monday\nadd buffer 10 minutes default all new meetings\nset buffer default 10 minutes amber\nthanks, typo sweep done and the defaults are kinder!\nCHUNK_EOF\nwc -l /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-calendar.txt && sort /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-calendar.txt | uniq -d",
