    "relatedEntryId": null,
    "type": "reasoning",
    "text": "Calendar done: 600, 0 duplicates. Now the document file. Mark todo in progress. Chunk 1 ~200 lines via write_file.\n\nDocument vocabulary: headings, paragraphs, lists, tables, columns, rows, fonts, styles, TOC, index, footnotes, citations, bibliography, page numbers, margins, headers/footers, captions, quotes, code blocks, spacing, indentation, alignment, bold/italic/underline, strikethrough, highlight, comments, track changes, spellcheck, grammar, word count, sections, chapters, appendices, figure, cross-references, styles (Normal, Heading 1), fonts (serif/sans), sizes, colors, templates, cover page, abstract, executive summary, revision history.\n\nCat 8: \"heading Intro level 3 bold\", \"set style body 11 regular\", \"set heading Methods level 2 italic\".\n\nCat 6 noun/verb: \"table the appendix summary\", \"figure the figure numbering\"? \"index the index terms\"? \"foot the page with the document title\", \"head each chapter with an epigraph\", \"top the page with the title\", \"bottom out\"? \"letter the captions\", \"number the chapters\", \"mark the marketing section\"? \"left align\" — \"left the margin\"? \"right the wrong\"? \"book the...\"? \"note the change\"? \"draft the draft\"? \"list the list of figures\" (list as verb + list as noun), \"table the table of contents\"? weird but fun: \"quote the quote at the top\" (quote as verb + quote as noun), \"style the style guide\"? \"caption the captions\"? \"section the second part\"? (section as verb), \"indent the indents\"? \"space the spacing\"? \"title the title page\"? good. \"page the document\"? \"watermark the...\"? \"cross the cross reference\"? \"bookmark the...\"? \"highlight the highlights\"? \"comment the comments\"? Use: list the list of figures, quote the opening quote, title the title page, section the appendix, foot the table, head each chapter, number the figures, letter the appendices, table the comparison, mark the margin? \"crop\"? Keep.\n\nTypos: \"pleese make the cloumns wider\" (given example — for document!), \"recieve\", \"seperate\", \"definately\", \"occured\", \"beleive\", \"wich\", \"thier\", \"teh\", \"hvae\", \"alot\", \"wierd\", \"untill\", \"accross\", \"begining\", \"writting\", \"proff\", \"sentance\".\n\nMissing words: \"make heading bold\", \"add table contents\", \"set font 12\", \"move paragraph up\", \"delete second row\", \"indent quote 2\".\n\nMeasures: \"make the margins 2.5 cm\", \"set columns two\", \"the table four columns wide\", \"font size 12\", \"line spacing 1.5\", \"page size A4\", \"150 words max\", \"set heading spacing 18 before 6 after\", \"x 120 y 40\" position for an image.\n\nLong lists after participle: \"cut the preamble down to a paragraph mentioning the scope, the method, the findings, and one caveat\", participial: \"an abstract stating the problem, a summary listing the results, a figure showing the trend, and a table holding the numbers\".\n\nOrder words: \"reorder the chapters, methods first then results\", \"highest first\" for sorting tables, \"then\", \"next\", \"instead\", \"again\", \"this time\".\n\nEmbedded questions: \"tell me where the conclusion went\", \"show what changed after the edit\", \"can you check what the current style is\".\n\nWrite ~200 lines chunk 1.",
