        "content": "make the title bold and centered\npleese make the cloumns wider\nheading Intro level 3 bold\nset style body 11 regular 1.5 spacing\ntell me where the conclusion went\ncan you show what changed after my last edit\nadd an abstract stating the problem, a paragraph listing the three findings, a figure showing the trend, and a table holding the raw numbers\nthen drop a caption under the figure: monthly totals, 2025\nset caption 9 point gray centered\nwhat if the abstract were half as long — try it\nthanks!\ncould you turn the bullet list into a numbered one\nhighest first: sort the rows in the results table by the last column\nthen relabel the columns: item, count, share\ninstead of share call it percentage\nagain with one decimal this time\nset results table header bold shaded light gray\nline the numbers up right aligned, the text left\nI wonder if the table needs a total row\ndrop in a footnote about the data source\nset footnote 8 point superscript\nthat would help.\nmkae the margins 2.5 cm all round\nwhere is the page number? add one bottom center\nset page numbers bottom center small\nthen suppress it on the title page\nnext add a header with the chapter name\nset header italic 9 point hairline below\nagain no hairline this time\nshow what changed in print preview\nthanks, layout finally behaves!\nhvae the document open on the styles pane\nset font body serif headings sans\ncan you set the whole report to A4 portrait\nthen make the appendix landscape only\nset appendix landscape margins 2 cm\ntell me how many words the intro is\nwhat if we cut ten percent of it everywhere\nagain only the intro this time\nI wonder if the passive voice should go\nmkae the first sentence shorter, it drags\nline the block quote up indented from both sides\ninstead of both sides indent only the left\nset block quote italic gray 11 point\nthanks!\ndefinately seperate the methods from the results, they blur\nadd a chapter between them called approach\nset heading approach level 2\ncan you renumber all the headings after it\ntell me which cross references broke\nthen fix them all in one pass\nhighest first: list the broken references by how far they point\nset cross references auto update\nnext rebuild the table of contents\nset TOC levels 1 to 3 dotted leaders\npleese make the cloumns of the TOC line up with the page numbers\nthat would help the reader a lot.\nthanks a lot!\nalot of typos, run the spellcheck and list them\nrecieve is spelled wrong twice, fix both\nwich and thier too, they keep slipping in\nuntill has two ls until the end, everywhere\naccross the document it should be across\nbegining should be beginning, chapter two mostly\nmkae teh running head say appendix, not abend\nset running head appendix roman numerals\ncan you turn off spellcheck for the code blocks\nthen leave it on everywhere else\nagain include the captions this time\ntell me how many words the whole thing is now\nI wonder if 9000 words is too many for this format\nline the corrections up in a change list I can approve\ninstead of approving each, accept all but the ones with names\nshow what changed after the sweep\nnext freeze the vocab list in the glossary\nset glossary alphabetical two columns\nthanks, clean text at last!\ntable the comparison of the three vendors in the appendix\ncan you give it four columns: name, price, support, notes\nset comparison table compact header bold\nthen shade the winning row pale green\nset winning row pale green bold name\nagain no bold this time, just the shade\ntell me which column is narrowest\ndrop in a note under the table: prices as of March\nset table note 8 point gray\nline the header cells up centered\ninstead of centered left align the notes column only\nshow what changed to the appendix\nnext move the table before the references, not after\nI wonder if landscape suits a four column table\nmkae the appendix table landscape, rest portrait\nthanks, the vendor bit is readable!\ncould you add a figure of the pipeline right after the methods\nset figure pipeline width 14 cm centered\nthen cross reference it from the results paragraph\nset cross reference figure 1 on page 3\nagain make it a page reference too this time\ntell me where figure 2 currently sits\nhighest first: order the figures by page distance from their first mention\nline the figure captions up flush left, not centered\ninstead of flush left center them all again\nshow what changed to the figures\nnext add a list of figures after the TOC\nset list of figures dotted leaders like the TOC\npleese make the cloumns of the lists of figures and tables identical\nI wonder if the list should skip tiny margin figures\nmkae any figure under 5 cm skip the list\nthanks, front matter complete!\nthat would help.\nhvae the comments show inline instead of balloons\nset comments inline author colored\ncan you resolve all the editor comments from last week\nthen leave mine open, they are reminders\nagain resolve mine too this time, the doc ships Friday\ntell me who left the longest comment thread\ndrop in a comment on the budget paragraph for finance\nset comment finance assign Priya\nline the resolved comments up in the history\ninstead of hiding them gray them out\nshow what changed since the review round\nnext export a version with all comments stripped\nset export clean pdf no comments no tracking\nI wonder if the tracked changes leak into the pdf\nmkae sure they do not, double check\nthanks, review round closed!\nfoot each page of the appendix with the document code\nset footer appendix code left page number right\ncan you head each chapter with its epigraph in italic\nset epigraph italic right aligned 10 point\nthen add a small attribution line under each\nset attribution 8 point small caps\nagain no small caps this time\ntell me which chapters lack epigraphs\nhighest first: list the chapters by how many pages they run\nline the chapter openers up: number, title, epigraph, drop three\ninstead of a drop put a faint rule after each title\nshow what changed to the chapter pages\nnext make chapter one open without a number\nset chapter one unnumbered but in the TOC\npleese make the cloumns of the epigraphs consistent in width\nI wonder if the epigraphs earn their space at all\nmkae them optional per chapter, flag the weak ones\nthanks, bookish in a good way!\nlist the list of figures again, it lost the last two entries\nset list of figures refresh auto\ncan you also rebuild the index terms\nthen mark the index subentries by category\nset index two levels indented\nagain three levels this time, the doc is deep\ntell me how many index entries we have\ndrop in the appendix letters instead of numbers\nset appendix lettered A B C D\nline the index leaders up like the TOC\ninstead of dotted use a thin space before the numbers\nshow what changed to the back matter\nnext hide the index while we still edit heavily\nset index hidden until final pass\nI wonder if the glossary and index should merge\nmkae them separate, cross link the overlaps\nthanks, navigation works now!\ntitle the title page in small caps, subtitle below in italic\nset title page small caps subtitle italic 14 point\ncan you center everything on the title page vertically too\nthen add the author line and the date at the bottom\nset author line centered date below\nagain no date this time, it ages badly\ntell me what the cover currently says\ndrop in a version box bottom right: v0.9 draft\nset version box gray small bordered\nline the dedication on its own page after the cover\ninstead of after the cover put it before the preface\nshow what changed to the front matter\nnext add a colophon at the very end\nset colophon 8 point centered small\npleese make the cloumns of the copyright page invisible, just text\nI wonder if the subtitle is too clever by half\nmkae the subtitle plainer: a practical guide\nthanks, the cover stops apologizing!\nthat would help the first impression.\nsection the appendix into three parts with dividers\nset appendix parts divided thin rules\ncan you number the paragraphs in the spec, like a legal doc\nthen keep the numbers stable while I edit\nset paragraph numbers stable renumber on request only\nagain renumber now this time, the draft moved a lot\ntell me how deep the heading nesting goes\nhighest first: list headings by level and count\nline the spec sections up with two digit numbers\ninstead of two digits use letters for the top level\nshow what changed to the numbering scheme\nnext add a revision history table at the end\nset revision history table date author change\npleese make the cloumns of the history table date friendly\nI wonder if we need a changelog at all for a draft\nmkae it one row per day, collapsed by default\nthanks, spec is navigable!\n",
