    "text": "197. Need 403 more. Append chunk 2 of ~200 lines. Themes: track changes, templates, cover letter, CV/resume, report sections, executive summary, bullets vs prose, hyphenation, widows/orphans, keep-with-next, section breaks, multi-column layout, sidebar boxes, pull quotes, code blocks, syntax highlighting, inline styles vs named styles, find and replace with wildcards, regex-like asks, case changes (sentence case, title case), smart quotes, dashes (en/em), ellipses, spacing after punctuation, non-breaking spaces, ligatures? Also charts/figures inside docs, references formats (APA/IEEE), citation manager, merge documents, compare versions, redline, watermarks, print options, bookmarks, hyperlinks, table of authorities? Keep general.\n\nCat 6 items still unused for document: \"quote the opening quote\", \"index the key terms\", \"mark the margin\"? \"crop\"? \"draft the draft notice\"? \"level the headings\"? \"space the spacing\"? \"indent the indents\"? \"note the side note\"? \"page the document for print\"? \"book the reference\"? \"append the appendix\"? (append as verb + appendix noun — good!). \"sample the sample text\"? \"table the table\"? \"figure the figure numbering\" hmm. \"word the wordy sentence\" (word as verb!). \"sentence the run on sentence\" — \"sentence\" as verb is different meaning. \"word the slogan tighter\" nice. \"key the keywords bold\". \"case the heading in title case\" (case as verb!). \"dash the hyphens into en dashes\"? \"spell the checked words\"? \"hyphen the hyphenated\"? Use: append the appendix, quote the opening quote, word the tagline tighter, case the headings in title case, key the keywords bold, index the proper names, letter the sub items.\n\nWrite ~200 lines.",
