OC ignore run ins, levels 1 and 2 only\nthanks, structure reads clean!\nthat would help.\nquote the opening quote in italic with a rule under it\nset opening quote italic rule below thin\ncan you tie the quote to its source in the references\nthen make the tie a superscript marker\nset quote marker superscript reference 3\nagain use author date in brackets this time\ntell me which references are never cited\nhighest first: list the uncited references by age\nline the references in alphabetical order, hanging indent\ninstead of alphabetical sort by citation order\nshow what changed to the bibliography\nnext switch citations to author date style throughout\nset citation style author date consistent\npleese make the cloumns of the references flush with hanging indents\nI wonder if two citation styles got mixed\nmkae the style one hundred percent consistent, no maybes\nthanks, scholarship tidy!\nindex the proper names in the back, not every noun\nset index proper names page numbers\ncan you collapse the duplicate index entries under one head word\nthen promote the frequent sub entries to head words\nset index merge duplicates promote frequent\nagain keep the fine grained entries this time\ntell me how fat the index is in pages\ndrop in a see also chain for the process entries\nset see also italic indented\nline the index head words up bold\ninstead of bold make head words small caps\nshow what changed to the index pages\nnext cut the index by a third, drop the vanity entries\nset index trim vanity terms\nI wonder if the ebook index needs page anchors instead\nmkae the index anchor based for the ebook build\nthanks, back of the book works!\nset font code mono 9 with light gray background\ncan you keep the code blocks from hyphenating\nthen turn on soft wrap only, no scroll\nset code wrap soft no horizontal scroll\nagain shrink long lines to 80 columns this time\ntell me which code block overflows the page\ndrop in line numbers in the left gutter of the code\nset code line numbers gray right aligned\nline the code captions up as listing 1, listing 2\ninstead of listing use example\nshow what changed to the listings\nnext add syntax highlighting in muted colors\nset syntax colors muted comments green\npleese make the cloumns of the inline code not stretch tables\nI wonder if the tables with code cells need smaller font\nmkae the code cells 8 point mono\nthanks, technical sections hold together!\nthat would help the reviewers.\nkey the keywords bold on their first appearance\nset keywords bold first appearance only\ncan you add a glossary link on jargon at first use\nthen build the glossary from those links, sorted\nset glossary auto built from links alphabetical\nagain include acronyms this time, expanded on first use\ntell me which acronyms never got expanded\nhighest first: list jargon by how often it appears\nline the glossary entries up term bold definition regular\ninstead of one column make the glossary two columns\nshow what changed to the glossary pages\nnext add the glossary to the TOC, level one\nset TOC glossary entry level 1\nI wonder if the glossary should open the doc instead of the abstract\nmkae the order: cover, glossary, abstract, then the rest\nthanks, jargon demystified!\nspell out the numbers under ten in prose\nset number style prose under ten spelled\ncan you leave the numbers in tables and figures alone\nthen also leave the units and dates alone\nset exceptions tables figures units dates\nagain spell under one hundred this time, formal doc\ntell me where the style conflicts with itself\ndrop in a style sheet note at the top for future editors\nset style note comment only not printed\nline the numbers in prose consistent with the style\ninstead of the comment keep it as an unnumbered page\nshow what changed to chapter three\nnext normalize the dates to day month year\nset date format day month year prose\npleese make the cloumns of the dates in the log table equal\nI wonder if iso dates read too robot for prose\nmkae prose dates human, table dates iso\nthanks, numbers and dates coherent!\nCHUNK_EOF\nwc -l /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-document.txt"
