      "display": {
        "summary": "bash: cat >> /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-document.txt <<'CHUNK_EOF'\nset the last chapter in two columns with a rule between them\nset two columns rule thin gap 18\ncan you balance the columns on the final page\nthen let the first page flow naturally unbalanced\nset columns balance last page only\nagain balance everywhere this time\ntell me how the figures survive two column layout\ndrop in a full width figure that spans both columns\nset spanning figure full width caption centered\nline the column footnotes up per column, not per page\ninstead of per column restart them per chapter\nshow what changed to the back pages\nnext widen the gutter to 20 for print\nset gutter 20 print safe\npleese make the cloumns of the newsletter grid snap to the baseline\nI wonder if three columns is too tight at this width\nmkae it two columns, larger type, calmer\nthanks, spread looks like a magazine!\nthat would help the print shop.\nwhere does the footnote numbering restart? it should be per page\nset footnotes restart per page\ncan you convert the footnotes to endnotes at the end of the book\nthen merge the endnotes into a single numbered list\nset endnotes single list continuous\nagain split by chapter this time, easier to check\ntell me how many footnotes we are carrying\nhighest first: chapters by footnote count\nline the endnote numbers up superscript in text\ninstead of superscript try bracketed numbers\nshow what changed to the apparatus\nnext strip the notes from the ebook version\nset ebook no endnotes link instead\nI wonder if readers click through at all, keep them anyway\nmkae the endnotes hyperlinked in the ebook only\nthanks, scholarly and digital!\nhvae my cv fit two pages without tiny type\nset cv two pages 10.5 point compact\ncan you lead with the last three roles only\nthen summarize the early ones in two lines each\nset early roles two lines summary\nagain one line each this time, they are ancient\ntell me which bullet is the weakest in the whole cv\ndrop in the promotion under each role, right aligned dates\nset dates right aligned promotion bold\nline the skills section up in three groups\ninstead of a skills list make it a short paragraph\nshow what changed to page one\nnext put the education last, nobody asks anymore\nset education last two lines\npleese make the cloumns of the cv dates align perfectly\nI wonder if a photo is expected here, leave it out\nmkae the header minimal: name, role, contacts on one line\nthanks, recruiters can skim it now!\ncould you draft a cover letter from the job ad, 200 words max\nset cover letter 200 words three paragraphs\ncan you open with the referral, not the role\nthen echo the three must haves in order\nset must haves one paragraph each mapped\nagain weave them through all three paragraphs this time\ntell me how many cliches you counted, be honest\ndrop in one concrete number per paragraph, nothing vague\nset numbers concrete metric bold\nline the closing paragraph up with a clear ask\ninstead of a weak ask end with availability dates\nshow what changed to the letter\nnext save it as a plain text version too, no formatting\nset plain text version no formatting attached\npleese make the cloumns of the two versions match content exactly\nI wonder if the tone is too eager\nmkae it confident, drop every exclamation mark\nthanks, letter reads like a human!\nthat would help the application.\nset heading Results level 2 bold\nset heading Methods level 2 italic\nset heading Discussion level 1 bold caps\nset style caption 9 gray\nset style quote 11 italic indented\nset paragraph lead 12 wider spacing\nset table header bold shaded\nset figure caption below not above\nset appendix roman numerals\nset TOC depth 2\ncan you apply those styles everywhere without touching the wording\nthen check no local formatting survived\nset local formatting strip all\nagain keep local bold on emphasis words this time\ntell me which paragraphs still fight the styles\nline the named styles up in the styles pane, alphabetical\ninstead of alphabetical sort by usage frequency\nshow what changed to the styles report\nnext save the whole set as a template called report clean\nset template report clean saved\nI wonder if the template should ship with placeholder text\nmkae the placeholder text obvious, lorem is lazy\nthanks, template is a real starting point!\nmkae teh heading say conclution then fix it to conclusion\npleese make the cloumns equaly wide in the budget table\nits supose to be twelve point not eleven, the body I mean\nhvae the intro say why now, not just why\nwritting style drifts formal to chatty around chapter four, smooth it\nthier are two blank pages before the appendix, remove them\nbeleive me the margins look different on the last page, check\nwierd spacing after every period, double spaces maybe, kill them\nmov the summary before the toc, it reads better first\nadd table contents right after title page\nset font 12 body no exceptions\nindent quote 2 from left\ndelete second row of the timeline table\nmake heading small caps not full caps\nthanks, cleanup pass done!\nthat would help before the editor sees it.\ncan you split chapter two at the case study\nthen promote the case study to a chapter of its own\nset case study chapter level 1\nagain keep it as a section this time, revert\ntell me how the page count moved after the split\nhighest first: order the chapters by how much they shrank in review\nline the new chapter transitions up, each opens with a bridge\ninstead of a bridge let two open cold, dramatic\nshow what changed to the outline\nnext update the TOC and the reading order note\nset reading order note preface updated\npleese make the cloumns of the outline view show word counts\nI wonder if the outline hides any empty sections\nmkae the empty sections visible with a placeholder dot\nthanks, structure visible at a glance!\ncould you package the final as pdf, epub and docx from one source\nset export three formats from one source\nthen name them consistently with the version number\nset file names report v1 0 consistent\nagain bump to v1 1 this time, we changed the cover\ntell me which format lost the fonts on export\ndrop in a pdf export preset: tagged, outlines off, images 300\nset pdf preset tagged fonts embedded\nline the three exports up in the delivery folder\ninstead of one folder split by recipient\nshow what changed in the delivery folder\nnext email the docx to Priya and keep the pdf for the board\nset delivery Priya docx board pdf\nI wonder if the epub passed the checker, run it again\nmkae the epub check part of the export, every time\nthanks, shipping is one click now!\nhvae the invoice table compute the vat line automatically\nset invoice vat 20 percent computed\ncan you total the columns at the bottom in bold\nthen carry the total to the summary box at the top\nset summary box total bold large\nagain round the total this time, whole numbers only\ntell me which line items lack a code\ndrop in a payment terms line under the table: net 30\nset payment terms net 30 small\nline the amounts up right aligned with the currency symbol consistent\ninstead of trailing symbol put it before, this is not a menu\nshow what changed to the invoice\nnext duplicate the invoice as a template with blanks\nset invoice template blanks no totals\npleese make the cloumns of the invoice template match the sample\nI wonder if the logo should sit left or centered\nmkae the logo left, quieter, same gray as the footer\nthanks, invoicing looks grown up!\nthat would help getting paid.\nmerge the two source docs into one report, keep the better intro\nset merge prefer doc one intro\ncan you deduplicate the references after the merge\nthen renumber the citations in the merged text\nset citations renumber sequential\nagain keep author date, no renumber this time\ntell me how many duplicates the merge created\nhighest first: list the duplicated passages by length\nline the merged sections up in one consistent voice\ninstead of my voice aim for the style guide voice\nshow what changed after the merge\nnext run a consistency pass on units, metric everywhere\nset units metric consistent\npleese make the cloumns of the merged tables share one header style\nI wonder if either source had a hidden section\nmkae the hidden sections visible, then delete them with my approval\nthanks, one document from two histories!\nwhere is the preface supposed to sit? before the TOC feels right\ncan you move the preface after the cover but before everything else\nset preface order cover then preface\nthen date the preface with month and year only\nset preface dated month year city optional\nagain no city this time, it felt presumptuous\ntell me who the acknowledgments currently thank\ndrop in a line thanking the pilot readers by group\nset acknowledgments pilot readers group anonymous\nline the acknowledgments up as one flowing paragraph\ninstead of one paragraph use short stanzas per group\nshow what changed to the front matter again\nnext keep the acknowledgments to one page maximum\nset acknowledgments one page max\npleese make the cloumns of the dedication centered by eye\nI wonder if a preface and an intro are redundant here\nmkae the preface personal, the intro technical, clear split\nthanks, front matter earns its pages at last!\nCHUNK_EOF\nwc -l /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-document.txt && sort /home/salboaie/work/sopworlds/webmeet-dataset/imported/generated/generated-document.txt | uniq -d",
