    "text": "Fix cross-file duplicates. Keep the drawing file versions; modify the others. Also \"thanks a lot!\" appears in 4 files — keep one (drawing), change 3. Plan replacements (check none of these strings already exist anywhere):\n\n- diagram:17 \"show what changed\" -> \"show what changed here\"\n- diagram:21 \"thanks a lot!\" -> \"thanks, that is a huge help!\" ; calendar:37 -> \"thanks, big help!\"; document:58 -> \"thanks, appreciate it!\"\n- diagram:70 \"thanks!\" -> \"thanks, brilliant!\"; calendar:12 -> \"thanks, perfect!\"; — wait \"thanks, perfect!\" exists in diagram:113 and drawing:205. So for calendar use \"thanks, wonderful!\"; document:11 -> \"thanks, great work!\"\n- diagram:113 \"thanks, perfect!\" -> keep diagram, change drawing:205 -> \"thanks, just right!\" (drawing). Since drawing is my \"keep\" file, but \"thanks, perfect!\" I said keep diagram... simpler: change drawing:205 to \"thanks, just right!\"\n- diagram:52 \"that is all; save it\" -> \"that is all; save the diagram\"; drawing:252 keep \"that is all; save it\"\n- calendar:72 \"that would help a lot.\" -> \"that would help the week a lot.\"; diagram:132 -> \"that would help the layout a lot.\"; drawing:226 keep.\n- \"that would help.\": keep drawing:39; calendar:23 -> \"that would help a lot.\"; wait calendar:72 was just changed to \"that would help the week a lot.\" — then calendar:23 can become... but \"that would help a lot.\" must not exist elsewhere: diagram:132 gets changed to \"that would help the layout a lot.\", drawing:226 keeps \"that would help a lot.\". So calendar:23 cannot be \"that would help a lot.\" — use \"that would help, truly.\"; document:22 -> \"that would help, I think.\"; diagram:20 -> \"that would help, I bet.\"\n\nCheck uniqueness of new strings across files: none exist now. Apply.",
