    "type": "reasoning",
    "text": "Wait — uniq -f1 with the \"file|line\" format: field separator is whitespace by default, and the filename contains no space, so -f1 skips the filename field. It reported 0 duplicates. But careful: uniq -f1 -d compares from field 2 onwards, but lines must be sorted by that. I sorted by -t'|' -k2 which sorts by the text after the pipe. The filename field ends at the pipe, not whitespace... -f1 splits on whitespace, but there's no whitespace between filename|line. So field 1 = \"file|line\" entire line, meaning uniq -f1 compares nothing? Actually with -f1 it skips field 1 which is the whole line (no spaces), so comparison is of empty strings → all lines equal → -d would print everything after first... it printed 0, which is suspicious. Let me redo properly with a space separator.",
    "summary": [],
    "outcome": {
      "type": "committed"
    }
  },
