        "text": "Done. Four files in the current folder, 600 lines each, 2,400 total:\n\n- `generated-drawing.txt` — 600\n- `generated-diagram.txt` — 600\n- `generated-calendar.txt` — 600\n- `generated-document.txt` — 600\n\nVerification results:\n- `wc -l` confirms exactly 600 per file, 2,400 total.\n- Zero duplicate lines — checked both within each file and across all four files combined (repeats like \"thanks!\" variants that cropped up during generation were rewritten to unique phrasings).\n- No empty lines, no trailing whitespace, no leading quotes or numbering; shortest lines are 7 chars, longest around 140 chars (3–45 words).\n\nCoverage is spread across all the requested constructions in every file: long comma lists after participles (\"a girl kneeling by the pond, two ducks on the water, a cat and a dog under the tree\"), measures and pairings (\"make it 160 wide and 100 high\", \"x 120 y 40\", \"10^1 to 10^6\"), order/time words (\"highest first\", \"then\", \"again\", \"this time\", \"instead\"), embedded and direct questions plus \"can you\"/\"could you\"/\"what if\"/\"I wonder if\" with commands, semicolon/dash/colon compounds and comments after a full stop (\"That would help.\", \"Thanks!\" variants), noun-as-verb and verb-as-noun traps (\"line Stove and Fridge up\", \"top the tower\", \"drop in an aqualung\", \"book the book club room\", \"spring the clocks forward\", \"table the rota discussion\"), realistic typos and missing words (\"pleese make the cloumns wider\", \"hvae the dog look at the cat\", \"its suposed to be twelve point\"), and names/values after nouns (\"set node Backup brown large\", \"heading Intro level 3 bold\", \"set event standup 9am recurring daily\").\n\nOne note: line lengths skew toward the middle of the 3–45 word range; only a minority sit at the extremes (3–5 words or 35+), which matches how users actually type."
